 61V  c  Compiled (unevaluated) data set from 2011Da08:                         
 61V 2c  Phys Rev C 83, 054312 (2011)                                           
 61V  c  Compiled by M. Birch and B. Singh (McMaster); May 19 {I2011}.          
 61V  c  {+61}V produced in the fragmentation of 57.8 MeV/nucleon {+86}Kr       
 61V 2c  beam impinged on 50 mg/cm{+2} thick tantalum target using LISE-2000    
 61V 3c  spectrometer at GANIL facility. Detector system included a             
 61V 4c  three-element Si-detector telescope containing a double-sided          
 61V 5c  silicon-strip detector (DSSSD) backed by a Si(Li) detector and         
 61V 6c  surrounded by four clover type EXOGAM Ge detectors. Product            
 61V 7c  identified by mass, atomic number, charge, energy loss and time of     
 61V 8c  flight. Measured half-life.                                            
 61V   L 0                               52.6 MS   42                           
 61V  cL T$ based on time correlation between implantation and |b-ray events    
 61V 2cL in the DSSSD. Fitting procedure included five parameters: |b-detection 
 61V 3cL efficiency, background rate, mother, daughter and granddaughter        
 61V 4cL half-lives (2011Da08)                                                  
                                                                                
